@DavidRBellamy Really appreciate you writing this. My impression is that the people who are scared that a single AI actor killing everyone via a virus will happen very, very late in the intelligence explosion. IIUC, the threat model is something like: the entire economy is run by AIs via APIs, robotics has also been solved, there is a renaissance in science and wet lab research because the embodied ASIs are running the whole lab, but at this point, humans are not able to oversee the AIs, so the embodied ASI end-to-end manufactures the virus and then releases it.

Now, that requires being very late in the intelligence explosion. I think ppl believe that the nearer-term risk is that the cognitive ASI convinces or pays humans in a wet lab to do the experimentation themselves and then release it. Though I don't buy this story because  I don't know enough about the threat model, and it feels capital-W weird.

Anyway, that's my attempt at steelmanning; curious for your takes
